IMPORT prelude

-- Strategic Goods (Control) Act 2002 (Singapore) -- what counts as a controlled movement (s 2), the ban on transferring strategic
-- goods and technology and the "catch-all" for weapons of mass destruction (s 5), brokering (s 6), appeals on permits and
-- registration (ss 7(5), 8(4)), the penalties (ss 5(7), 6(9), 9, 10(2), 11(4), 12(3), 18(2), 20, 30), composition (s 31), officers
-- of bodies corporate (s 32(1)) and the 48-hour limit on detention after arrest (s 21(5)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SGCA2002.txt. The cover says
-- the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December
-- 2021"; the page furniture reads "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 1/7/2025", and the latest amendment annotated is
-- Act 3 of 2021 (Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021, commenced 1 July 2025), which repealed s 3.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0087 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the duties a trader, forwarder, researcher or broker meets and what breaking them costs. Not encoded:
-- what is on the strategic goods list (s 4A -- the list is a Ministerial order, not in the deposit), Ministerial declarations
-- (s 35) and exemptions (s 36), the permit and registration regulations (ss 7(7), 8(6)), search, seizure and arrest powers beyond
-- the 48-hour limit (ss 14 to 21), confidentiality conditions for foreign authorities (s 12(2)), proceedings (ss 22 to 29) and
-- the regulation-making power (s 38).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive rows (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not loadable in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Strategic Goods (Control) Act 2002 -- transfers and brokering`

§§ `2 -- what is a controlled movement`

-- s 2(1): "export" means "to take out from Singapore goods ... but does not include the taking out from Singapore of goods that have
-- been brought in transit or transhipped". "bring in transit" means to bring goods into Singapore "where the goods are to be taken
-- out from Singapore on the same conveyance ... without any landing in Singapore, but does not include the passage through
-- Singapore in accordance with international law of a foreign conveyance carrying goods". "tranship" means to move goods to the
-- same or another conveyance "on a through bill of lading, through airway bill or through manifest".
-- s 2(2): passage in accordance with international law means passing "without stopping or anchoring in Singapore except in a
-- situation of distress"; a conveyance is foreign "if it is not registered in Singapore".
-- s 5(1)(a) bans export, transhipment and bringing in transit. The Act controls nothing about IMPORT.
DECLARE Movement IS ONE OF
    `taking goods out of Singapore after they were landed here`
    `transhipping goods on a through bill of lading`
    `carrying goods through a Singapore port on the same ship without landing them`
    `a foreign ship passing through Singapore waters without stopping`
    `a foreign ship anchoring in Singapore only in distress`
    `importing goods into Singapore`

GIVEN `the movement` IS A Movement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the movement is controlled by section 5(1)(a)` IF
    CONSIDER `the movement`
    WHEN `a foreign ship passing through Singapore waters without stopping` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a foreign ship anchoring in Singapore only in distress` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `importing goods into Singapore` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5 -- transfer of strategic goods and technology`

-- s 5(1): a person must not (a) "export, tranship or bring in transit any strategic goods"; (b) export a document recording
-- strategic goods technology; or (c) "transmit any strategic goods technology".
-- s 5(2): the same for ANY goods or technology if (d) the person "has been notified by an authorised officer" that they are
-- intended or likely to be used for a "relevant activity" (nuclear, chemical or biological weapons, or missiles to deliver them);
-- (e) the person "knows" they are intended to be so used; or (f) "has reasonable grounds to suspect" it.
-- (3): neither applies to "an act authorised by a permit". (4): nor to "technology in the public domain". (5): nor to exporting a
-- technology document or transmitting technology "to the extent that this is necessary to facilitate" (a) installing, operating,
-- maintaining or repairing goods lawfully moved, (b) "an application for a patent", or (c) research "the results of which have no
-- practical application".
-- (6): "Subsection (2)(a) does not apply to the bringing in transit of any goods with the approval of a senior authorised officer."
-- That approval lifts only the catch-all; it does not lift s 5(1) for listed strategic goods.
-- (8): for a transmission, a defence if the accused "did not know nor have reason to believe" it would become accessible to a
-- person in a foreign country. (9): for (2)(f) only, a defence if the accused "made all reasonable inquiries" and was satisfied
-- the goods or technology will not be so used.
DECLARE Transfer HAS
    `the item is technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act is a transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act is bringing in transit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the item is prescribed as strategic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notified by an officer of a weapons use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows of a weapons use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has reasonable grounds to suspect a weapons use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by a permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the technology is in the public domain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `necessary for servicing, a patent or research of no practical application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `transit approved by a senior authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved reasonable inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved no reason to believe it would reach a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is excused under section 5(3) to (5)` IF
        `the transfer`'s `authorised by a permit`
    OR  (    `the transfer`'s `the item is technology`
         AND (    `the transfer`'s `the technology is in the public domain`
              OR  `the transfer`'s `necessary for servicing, a patent or research of no practical application`))

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the catch-all can apply` IF
    NOT (`the transfer`'s `the act is bringing in transit` AND `the transfer`'s `transit approved by a senior authorised officer`)

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is caught by notice or knowledge` IF
        `the catch-all can apply` `the transfer`
    AND (`the transfer`'s `notified by an officer of a weapons use` OR `the transfer`'s `knows of a weapons use`)

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is caught by suspicion` IF
        `the catch-all can apply` `the transfer`
    AND `the transfer`'s `has reasonable grounds to suspect a weapons use`

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer contravenes section 5` IF
        (NOT `the transfer is excused under section 5(3) to (5)` `the transfer`)
    AND (    `the transfer`'s `the item is prescribed as strategic`
         OR  `the transfer is caught by notice or knowledge` `the transfer`
         OR  `the transfer is caught by suspicion` `the transfer`)

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is an offence under section 5` IF
        (NOT `the transfer is excused under section 5(3) to (5)` `the transfer`)
    AND (NOT (`the transfer`'s `the act is a transmission` AND `the transfer`'s `proved no reason to believe it would reach a foreign country`))
    AND (    `the transfer`'s `the item is prescribed as strategic`
         OR  `the transfer is caught by notice or knowledge` `the transfer`
         OR  (`the transfer is caught by suspicion` `the transfer` AND (NOT `the transfer`'s `proved reasonable inquiries`)))

§§ `5(7) and 6(9) -- penalty for transfer or brokering`

-- s 5(7) and s 6(9), in the same words: "(a) on a first conviction, to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or 3 times the value of the
-- goods or technology ..., whichever is the greater, or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both"; "(b) on a
-- second or subsequent conviction, to a fine not exceeding $200,000 or 4 times the value ..., whichever is the greater, or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both". s 2(4): the value is the value "at the time of the commission of the
-- offence".
GIVEN `first amount` IS A NUMBER, `second amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `first amount` AT LEAST `second amount` THEN `first amount` ELSE `second amount`

GIVEN `value of the goods or technology` IS A NUMBER, `is a first conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for transfer or brokering` MEANS
    IF `is a first conviction`
    THEN `the greater of` 100000 (3 TIMES `value of the goods or technology`)
    ELSE `the greater of` 200000 (4 TIMES `value of the goods or technology`)

GIVEN `is a first conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for transfer or brokering` MEANS
    IF `is a first conviction` THEN 2 ELSE 3

§§ `6 -- brokering`

-- s 6(1): a person must not "arrange or negotiate, or do any act to facilitate the arrangement or negotiation of" a contract to
-- acquire or dispose of goods (or acquire, dispose of or transmit technology) "if the person knows or has reason to believe" it
-- "will or is likely to result in the removal of those goods from one foreign country to another foreign country".
-- (2), (3): it applies to (a) strategic goods or technology "as the Minister may specify by order in the Gazette", and (b) any goods
-- or technology on notice, knowledge or reasonable suspicion of a weapons use.
-- (4): not to technology in the public domain. (5): not to an act about the Minister-specified GOODS "by a person who is
-- registered". (6): not to an act about catch-all goods, or about ANY technology in (3), "that is authorised by a permit".
-- So listed goods need registration and a permit does not help; listed technology needs a permit and registration does not help.
-- (7): not to a person whose "sole involvement" is transport, financing, insurance, or advertising "information that is generally
-- available to the public". (8): not to technology "necessary to facilitate" servicing abroad of goods "which are not strategic
-- goods", a patent application, or research with no practical application.
-- (10): for the reasonable-suspicion limbs only, a defence of "all reasonable inquiries".
DECLARE Brokering HAS
    `about technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specified by the Minister's order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notified by an officer of a weapons use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows of a weapons use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has reasonable grounds to suspect a weapons use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows or has reason to believe it moves between two foreign countries` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the broker is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by a permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the technology is in the public domain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sole involvement is transport, finance, insurance or public advertising` IS A BOOLEAN
    `technology necessary for a section 6(8) purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved reasonable inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the deal` IS A Brokering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6(1) reaches the deal` IF
        `the deal`'s `knows or has reason to believe it moves between two foreign countries`
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `sole involvement is transport, finance, insurance or public advertising`)
    AND (NOT (    `the deal`'s `about technology`
              AND (`the deal`'s `the technology is in the public domain` OR `the deal`'s `technology necessary for a section 6(8) purpose`)))

GIVEN `the deal` IS A Brokering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the listed limb is unexcused` IF
        `the deal`'s `specified by the Minister's order`
    AND (IF `the deal`'s `about technology`
         THEN NOT `the deal`'s `authorised by a permit`
         ELSE NOT `the deal`'s `the broker is registered`)

GIVEN `the deal` IS A Brokering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the brokering contravenes section 6` IF
        `section 6(1) reaches the deal` `the deal`
    AND (    `the listed limb is unexcused` `the deal`
         OR  (    (NOT `the deal`'s `authorised by a permit`)
              AND (    `the deal`'s `notified by an officer of a weapons use`
                   OR  `the deal`'s `knows of a weapons use`
                   OR  `the deal`'s `has reasonable grounds to suspect a weapons use`)))

GIVEN `the deal` IS A Brokering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the brokering is an offence under section 6` IF
        `section 6(1) reaches the deal` `the deal`
    AND (    `the listed limb is unexcused` `the deal`
         OR  (    (NOT `the deal`'s `authorised by a permit`)
              AND (    `the deal`'s `notified by an officer of a weapons use`
                   OR  `the deal`'s `knows of a weapons use`
                   OR  (`the deal`'s `has reasonable grounds to suspect a weapons use` AND (NOT `the deal`'s `proved reasonable inquiries`)))))

§§ `7(5) and 8(4) -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 7(5): "A person aggrieved by a decision of the Director-General not to grant or renew a permit, or to cancel a permit, may appeal
-- to the Minister whose decision is final." s 8(4): the same for a decision "not to register the person or renew the person's
-- registration, or to cancel or suspend the person's registration". Neither subsection lists the conditions imposed under
-- s 7(3) or 8(2).
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusing a permit`
    `refusing to renew a permit`
    `cancelling a permit`
    `imposing conditions on a permit`
    `refusing registration`
    `suspending a registration`
    `imposing conditions on a registration`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision may be appealed to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `imposing conditions on a permit` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `imposing conditions on a registration` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `9, 10, 11, 12, 18, 20, 30 -- the other offences`

-- s 9 breach of a prescribed condition of a permit or registration "without lawful excuse": $50,000 or 12 months.
-- s 10(2) failing "without reasonable cause" to give particulars, keep records or give reports: $10,000 or 6 months.
-- s 11(4) failing to comply with a senior authorised officer's written notice for information or documents: $10,000 or 6 months.
-- s 12(3) publishing or disclosing information given under Part 3 without consent: $6,000 or 12 months.
-- s 18(2) refusing access to or assistance with a computer during a search: $10,000 or 6 months.
-- s 20 obstructing or refusing access or assistance to an officer "without lawful excuse": $10,000 or 6 months.
-- s 30(1) false or misleading information or documents in an application or under Part 3: $50,000 or 12 months; (2) defence of
-- "all reasonable steps to ascertain ... the truth".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `breaching a permit or registration condition`
    `failing to give particulars, keep records or report`
    `ignoring a notice to give information`
    `disclosing information given under Part 3`
    `refusing help with a computer during a search`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `giving false or misleading information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breaching a permit or registration condition` THEN 50000
    WHEN `disclosing information given under Part 3` THEN 6000
    WHEN `giving false or misleading information` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breaching a permit or registration condition` THEN 12
    WHEN `disclosing information given under Part 3` THEN 12
    WHEN `giving false or misleading information` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 6

§§ `31 -- composition`

-- s 31(1): a senior authorised officer "may compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by
-- collecting ... a sum not exceeding $10,000". The prescribed list is in regulations (s 31(2)), not in the deposit.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum collected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is within section 31` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum collected` AT MOST 10000

§§ `32(1) -- officers of a body corporate`

-- s 32(1): where a company's offence "is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to
-- any neglect on the part of an officer", "the officer as well as the body corporate shall be guilty of that offence".
GIVEN `the company committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the company committed an offence` AND (`the officer consented or connived` OR `attributable to the officer's neglect`)

§§ `21(5) -- detention after arrest without warrant`

-- s 21(3): the arrested person must be produced before a Magistrate "without unnecessary delay"; (4) not detained longer than "is
-- reasonable"; (5) "Such period must not exceed 48 hours, excluding the time for any necessary journey to the Magistrate's Court."
-- Only the outer 48-hour limit is encoded; reasonableness under (4) can cut it shorter.
GIVEN `hours in custody` IS A NUMBER, `hours of necessary journey` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detention is within the 48-hour limit` IF
    `hours in custody` MINUS `hours of necessary journey` AT MOST 48
